<title>GERMANY: FMC H1 net profit up 45 pct.</title>
<headline>FMC H1 net profit up 45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OBERURSEL, Germany 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in dollars)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			 $55 million   up 45 pct</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share	     $0.72     vs n/a</p>
<p>Group cash flow before tax</p>
<p>(earnings before interest, taxes,</p>
<p>    depreciation, amortisation)	  $333 million  up 24 pct</p>
<p>    Group sales			     $1.582 bln up 5 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the manufacturer of dialysis equipment is Fresenius Medical Care (FMC), majority-owned by Fresenius AG. FMC also said group sales rose eight percent if adjusted to exclude the impact of currency movements. Sales of core products -- dialysis products and services -- rose 12 percent if adjusted for currency movements.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
